# Project-Companion environment configuration.
#
# DEFAULT POSTURE: the prototype runs in MOCK TUTOR MODE — no network calls
# to any AI provider, no API key needed. This is the safe default for a
# child-facing prototype. The UI renders deterministic stub responses so
# you can demo the experience without risk.

# ============================================================
# LIVE MODE (developer testing only — DO NOT deploy to minors)
# ============================================================
#
# To test the live Anthropic integration during development, set BOTH:
#
#   VITE_TUTOR_ALLOW_LIVE_CLAUDE=true
#   VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#
# Live mode logs a loud red console warning on first call so it is
# impossible to forget you have live mode on. Because VITE_-prefixed env
# vars are embedded in the client bundle, ANY build with these set
# exposes the API key to anyone who loads the page. That is acceptable
# for solo developer testing on localhost; it is NOT acceptable for any
# deployment, especially one accessible to minors.
#
# The production-shaped path is to remove this client-side call entirely
# and replace it with a backend proxy that holds the key server-side and
# applies per-user rate limiting, audit logging, content moderation, and
# COPPA-compliant consent gating. See the README Roadmap.

# Default: mock mode (leave the line below commented or unset)
# VITE_TUTOR_ALLOW_LIVE_CLAUDE=true

# Only required if VITE_TUTOR_ALLOW_LIVE_CLAUDE=true
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here
